        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "Count carbons first. 1-bromopropane and propanoic acid both have three carbons, so the route must not add a carbon. Substitution with NaOH(aq) gives propan-1-ol, and heating a primary alcohol under reflux with acidified dichromate oxidises it to propanoic acid.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:15.1(3)",
                "syllabus:16.1(2)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "The KCN route adds a carbon: CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>Br → CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>CN, and hydrolysis of this nitrile gives butanoic acid (four carbons), not propanoic acid.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:19.2(3)",
                "syllabus:21.1(2)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "optionAnalysis": [
            {
              "key": "A",
              "correct": true,
              "text": "NaOH(aq) gives propan-1-ol; acidified dichromate under reflux oxidises it to propanoic acid. The chain stays at three carbons."
            },
            {
              "key": "B",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "Propan-1-ol does not react with CO<sub>2</sub> to give a carboxylic acid."
            },
            {
              "key": "C",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "KCN adds a carbon, giving butanenitrile; acid hydrolysis then gives butanoic acid, not propanoic acid."
            },
            {
              "key": "D",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "KCN adds a carbon, and alkaline hydrolysis of the nitrile gives sodium butanoate rather than propanoic acid."
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Start C<sub>3</sub>, finish C<sub>3</sub>: no carbon may be added, which rules out KCN (C and D).",
            "NaOH(aq): CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>Br → CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>OH.",
            "H<sup>+</sup>/Cr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>7</sub><sup>2–</sup>, reflux: CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>OH → CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>COOH.",
            "Option A."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": [
